 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Twenty dollars. For one pair of socks.",
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 2.636
  },
  {
   "text": "Hikers keep buying them anyway. Here's why.",
   "start": 2.886,
   "end": 5.577
  },
  {
   "text": "Merino fiber is so fine, it doesn't itch like normal wool.",
   "start": 5.977,
   "end": 9.578
  },
  {
   "text": "It's naturally odor-resistant, so you can wear it again on day two.",
   "start": 9.978,
   "end": 13.675
  },
  {
   "text": "And it stays warm, even when it's damp. Cotton doesn't.",
   "start": 14.075,
   "end": 17.363
  },
  {
   "text": "Cheap socks cost you the hike.",
   "start": 17.813,
   "end": 19.339
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next trek, and pick your color at the link in bio.",
   "start": 19.839,
   "end": 23.666
  }
 ],
